1
00:00:03,921 --> 00:00:05,589
HEY, REMEMBER
WHEN I HAD A MONKEY?

2
00:00:05,631 --> 00:00:06,841
YEAH.
MM-HMM.

3
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:09,468
YEAH, WHAT...
WHAT WAS I THINKING?

4
00:00:10,803 --> 00:00:13,555
HEY, SO...
WHAT'S WITH THE 20% TIP?

5
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:15,641
DID I DO SOMETHING WRONG?

6
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:19,102
20% IS A PRETTY
GENEROUS TIP, JOE.

7
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,480
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT'S
MORE GENEROUS THAN THAT? 50%.

8
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:22,940
YOU KNOW WHAT'S

9
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:24,399
EVEN MORE GENEROUS THAN THAT?

10
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,943
I SEE WHERE YOU'RE GOING.

11
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,029
WHAT'S UP
WITH THE GREED, JOE?

12
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,656
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I'M SORRY, YOU GUYS

13
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:32,199
BUT IT'S JUST
THAT I GOT TO GET

14
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,576
THESE NEW HEAD SHOTS MADE,
AND THEY'RE REALLY EXPENSIVE

15
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:35,577
YOU KNOW?

16
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:37,663
I'M DOWN TO, LIKE, THREE.

17
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:39,540
ACTUALLY, TWO
'CAUSE ONE OF THEM

18
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,500
I KIND OF BLACKENED IN
SOME TEETH.

19
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:42,793
WHY'D I DO THAT?

20
00:00:42,835 --> 00:00:44,003
GOD!

21
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:45,838
WELL, ISN'T THERE
SOMETHING YOU CAN DO

22
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,339
TO EARN A LITTLE
EXTRA MONEY?

23
00:00:47,381 --> 00:00:48,799
I MEAN, CAN'T
YOU PICK UP...

24
00:00:48,841 --> 00:00:50,509
I DON'T KNOW,
AN EXTRA SHIFT HERE?

25
00:00:50,551 --> 00:00:53,971
OR... YOU KNOW, I USED
TO BEG FOR MONEY.

26
00:00:55,556 --> 00:00:56,932
OF COURSE, IT HELPS

27
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:59,018
IF YOU'VE GOT A LITTLE
OF THIS GOING ON.

28
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,644
WOW. I STILL HAVE IT.

29
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:02,103
Joey:
YEAH.

30
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:04,314
OH, WAIT, WAIT. DON'T YOU
HAVE AN AUDITION TODAY?

31
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:05,900
YEAH, MAYBE
YOU'LL GET THAT JOB.

32
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:07,192
OH, HA, HA, HA.

33
00:01:07,234 --> 00:01:09,695
OOH!

34
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:12,239
WAIT A MINUTE-- I USED TO GET
MEDICAL EXPERIMENTS

35
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,532
DONE ON ME ALL THE TIME.

36
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:17,077
AH, FINALLY AN EXPLANATION.

37
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:18,537
NO, NO, I USED TO GET PAID

38
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:20,831
FOR ALL KINDS
OF MEDICAL STUFF, REMEMBER?

39
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:24,167
LET'S SEE, UH... WELL, I DON'T
WANT TO DONATE SPERM AGAIN.

40
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:27,170
I REALLY PREFER DOING THAT
AT THE HOME OFFICE, YOU KNOW.

41
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,088
OOH, OOH!

42
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:32,718
MAYBE THEY WANT SOME OF MY BLOOD
OR SPIT OR SOMETHING, HUH?
JOEY.

43
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:35,554
YEAH.
WHAT'D I TELL YOU
ABOUT TALKING TO YOUR FRIENDS

44
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:36,889
WHILE YOU'RE WORKING?

45
00:01:36,931 --> 00:01:39,224
UH... DO IT?

46
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:42,394
THAT GUY'S BEEN WAITING
FOR HIS COFFEE FOR TEN MINUTES.

47
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:44,605
HE'S COMPLAINED ABOUT YOU
THREE TIMES.

48
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:49,276
WELL, WHERE WAS I?

49
00:01:56,617 --> 00:02:01,914
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

50
00:02:01,956 --> 00:02:04,124
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

51
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,418
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

52
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:11,423
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

53
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:14,635
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

54
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,971
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

55
00:02:17,012 --> 00:02:20,181
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

56
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:26,187
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

57
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,359
HI.
HEY.

58
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:32,903
HEY, WHAT HAVE YOU
GUYS BEEN UP TO?

59
00:02:32,945 --> 00:02:34,738
OH, WE WENT TO A SELF-DEFENSE
CLASS TODAY.

60
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:35,781
WOW.
YEAH.

61
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:37,324
KICKING A GUY IN THE
CROTCH ALL MORNING

62
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:39,534
REALLY TAKES IT
OUT OF YOU.

63
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,996
TAKES IT OUT OF YOU?

64
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:44,539
NO, NOW WE CAN KICK
ANYBODY'S ASS.

65
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:45,666
YEAH.

66
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:46,834
AFTER ONE CLASS?

67
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,335
I DON'T THINK SO.

68
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,129
WHAT? YOU WANT TO SEE ME
SELF-DEFEND MYSELF?

69
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:52,506
GO OVER THERE AND PRETEND
YOU'RE A SEXUAL PREDATOR.

70
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,508
GO ON, I DARE YOU!

71
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,427
WELL, OF COURSE,
YOU CAN DEFEND YOURSELF

72
00:02:57,469 --> 00:03:00,014
FROM AN ATTACK
YOU KNOW IS COMING.

73
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,723
THAT'S NOT ENOUGH.

74
00:03:01,765 --> 00:03:05,435
LOOK, I STUDIED KAR-ATEY
FOR A LONG TIME

75
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:07,855
AND THERE'S
A CONCEPT

76
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:10,065
YOU SHOULD
REALLY BE FAMILIAR WITH.

77
00:03:10,107 --> 00:03:14,277
IT'S WHAT THE JAPANESE
CALL UNAGI.

78
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:18,032
ISN'T THAT A KIND OF SUSHI?

79
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:20,241
NO, IT'S A CONCEPT.

80
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:22,327
YEAH, IT IS. IT IS.
IT'S FRESHWATER EEL.

81
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:25,413
ALL RIGHT,
MAYBE IT MEANS THAT, TOO.

82
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:26,790
OH, I WOULD KILL

83
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:29,501
FOR A SALMON SKIN
ROLL RIGHT NOW.

84
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:32,129
YOU KNOW, FINE, GET ATTACKED;
I DON'T EVEN CARE.

85
00:03:32,171 --> 00:03:33,212
( sighs )

86
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:35,215
COME ON, ROSS. WE'RE SORRY.

87
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,176
PLEASE TELL US WHAT IT IS.

88
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:44,808
UNAGI IS A STATE
OF TOTAL AWARENESS, OKAY?

89
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:48,687
ONLY BY ACHIEVING TRUE UNAGI
CAN YOU BE PREPARED

90
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:51,982
FOR ANY DANGER
THAT MAY BEFALL YOU.

91
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:54,735
YOU MEAN, IN CASE
SOMEONE'S TRYING TO STEAL

92
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:57,863
YOUR BAMBOO SLEEPING MAT
OR YOUR KETTLE OF FISH?

93
00:03:57,905 --> 00:04:00,699
( mocking laughter )

94
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:03,702
ALL I'M SAYING IS,
IT'S ONE THING
BEING PREPARED

95
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:06,121
FOR AN ATTACK AGAINST,
LIKE, EACH OTHER.

96
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:09,041
WHOLE 'NOTHER STORY
BEING PREPARED
FOR AN ATTACK

97
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:10,918
I DON'T KNOW,
LIKE, A SURPRISE!

98
00:04:18,092 --> 00:04:20,677
ALL RIGHT, YOU KNEW
THAT WAS COMING

99
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:23,513
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN
YOU HAVE UNAGI.

100
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:27,017
OOH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

101
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,560
IF WE MADE RESERVATIONS

102
00:04:28,602 --> 00:04:30,771
WE COULD HAVE UNAGI
IN ABOUT A HALF HOUR.

103
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,022
YOU KNOW WHAT...?

104
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:35,609
HEY, HEY, IS MONICA HERE?

105
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,777
NO. UH-UH.

106
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:38,277
LOOK, I NEED YOUR HELP--
I DON'T KNOW

107
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:40,155
WHAT TO GET HER
FOR VALENTINE'S DAY.

108
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:42,866
WELL, VALENTINE'S DAY
WAS TWO WEEKS AGO

109
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:45,160
SO I WOULDN'T
GET HER A CALENDAR.

110
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:46,286
( weak chuckle )

111
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:47,871
SHE WAS WORKING
ON VALENTINE'S DAY

112
00:04:47,913 --> 00:04:49,456
SO WE'RE CELEBRATING
IT TONIGHT.

113
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:52,167
OH, HEY, WHY DON'T YOU
BOOK A DAY FOR BOTH OF YOU

114
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:53,835
AT ONE OF THOSE
ROMANTIC SPAS?

115
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:56,463
OOH, JOEY, THAT'S ACTUALLY
A REALLY GOOD IDEA.

116
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:58,924
YEAH, AND, OF COURSE,
CROTCHLESS PANTIES.

117
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:02,970
WELL, AS APPEALING

118
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,972
AS THAT DOES SOUND
TO HER BOYFRIEND...

119
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,223
AND HER BROTHER...

120
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:10,978
I CAN'T DO THAT.

121
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,480
WE PROMISED WE'D MAKE
EACH OTHER GIFTS THIS YEAR.

122
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:14,982
OH, I LOVE THAT.
YOU GUYS!

123
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,483
YOU CAN'T MAKE
CROTCHLESS PANTIES?

124
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:17,525
YOU TAKE...

125
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:21,029
YOU TAKE A PAIR OF SCISSORS
AND JUST CUT THE...

126
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:23,031
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY!

127
00:05:23,073 --> 00:05:25,617
SO, MAKING THINGS--
THAT SOUNDS SO MUCH FUN.

128
00:05:25,659 --> 00:05:26,994
YEAH, I THOUGHT SO, TOO

129
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,079
UNTIL I PAPIER-MACHE'D
ONE OF MY EYES SHUT.

130
00:05:29,121 --> 00:05:30,538
I LOVE PAPIER-MACHE.

131
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,915
WHAT DID YOU MAKE?

132
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:34,042
I MADE A ( gibberish ).

133
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:36,128
WHAT IS THAT?

134
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,171
NOTHING!
OH.

135
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,757
SO WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

136
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:42,217
WELL, HAVE YOU GUYS
MADE ANYTHING

137
00:05:42,259 --> 00:05:43,802
THAT MAYBE
I COULD TAKE CREDIT FOR?

138
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:45,179
OOH, I HAVE. I HAVE.

139
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,514
UM, I STARTED MAKING
THESE LITTLE SOCK BUNNIES.

140
00:05:47,555 --> 00:05:48,807
OH, FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

141
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:50,017
LOOK.

142
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,351
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

143
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:54,062
THAT IS MY SOCK.

144
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,524
NOW IT'S YOUR
LITTLE BUNNY FRIEND.

145
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:59,484
( both laughing )

146
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:09,703
OKAY.

147
00:06:14,249 --> 00:06:17,878
THIS... THIS ACTUALLY
IS A ( gibberish ).

148
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,420
HEY!

149
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:20,421
HEY.

150
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,798
HONEY, CAN I ASK YOU A QUESTION

151
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,258
ABOUT THE VALENTINE'S DAY GIFTS?

152
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,592
OH, YEAH.

153
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,053
DO WE HAVE TO MAKE
THE ENTIRE THING?

154
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,179
YES.

155
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:28,889
WHY, DID YOU FORGET
TO MAKE YOURS?

156
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,850
OF COURSE... OF COURSE NOT.

157
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,518
I JUST HAVE TO, UH...

158
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:36,395
GO OVER TO THE PLACE WHERE
I MADE IT AND PICK IT UP.

159
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:37,939
OKAY. I CAN'T WAIT.

160
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:40,399
THIS IS GOING TO BE
THE BEST VALENTINE'S DAY EVER.

161
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:41,526
( nervous laughter )

162
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:44,445
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

163
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:45,655
MAKE THE PRESENTS!

164
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:46,865
MAKE THE PRESENTS!

165
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,325
WHAT?

166
00:06:48,367 --> 00:06:51,410
I'M JUST SO EXCITED
TO MAKE THE PRESENTS!

167
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,496
( nervous laughter )

168
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:56,875
SHOOT!

169
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:01,963
HI. UH, I'M JOEY TRIBBIANI

170
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:03,257
AND, WITH ALL
DUE RESPECT

171
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:05,008
I'D LIKE TO
DONATE SOME FLUIDS.

172
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:09,263
WE'RE ACTUALLY AT THE END
OF ONE OF OUR RESEARCH CYCLES

173
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,472
SO WE'RE NOT LOOKING
FOR APPLICANTS RIGHT NOW.

174
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:14,309
OH, THAT'S TOO BAD;
I KIND OF BEEN SAVING UP.

175
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,106
UH... ARE YOU SURE

176
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,275
THERE'S NO STUDIES
I COULD PARTICIPATE IN?

177
00:07:21,316 --> 00:07:23,277
WELL, HERE'S A SCHEDULE
OF WHAT'S COMING UP.

178
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:24,945
AH, THANKS.

179
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,363
BUT THIS ONE
STARTS NOW.

180
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:28,740
OH, THAT ONE
IS AVAILABLE NOW

181
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:31,492
BUT ONLY IDENTICAL TWINS
ARE ELIGIBLE; IT'S A TWIN STUDY.

182
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:33,328
BUT IT'S $2,000.

183
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:34,829
SORRY.

184
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:37,040
OH.

185
00:07:37,082 --> 00:07:39,042
AND, WELL, HOW
ABOUT THIS ONE?

186
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:41,295
"TESTING THE EFFECTS
OF JOEY TRIBBIANI

187
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:43,713
ON ATTRACTIVE NURSE
RECEPTIONIST."

188
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:46,674
WE ALREADY GOT
THE RESULTS BACK ON THAT ONE

189
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:48,218
AND THEY'RE NOT GOOD.

190
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,141
...BUT IT WAS GOOD.

191
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:55,434
THOSE LAST MOVES WERE...

192
00:07:55,474 --> 00:07:57,477
DANGER! DANGER!

193
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:58,853
ROSS!

194
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:04,443
WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?!

195
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:08,738
A LESSON IN THE IMPORTANCE
OF UNAGI.

196
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,158
OH!

197
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:13,076
YOU'RE A FREAK!

198
00:08:13,118 --> 00:08:15,329
PERHAPS.

199
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:18,290
NOW, I'M CURIOUS--

200
00:08:18,332 --> 00:08:21,126
AT WHAT POINT
DURING THOSE GIRLISH SCREAMS

201
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:23,711
WOULD YOU HAVE BEGUN
TO "KICK MY ASS"?

202
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:28,591
ALL RIGHT, SO WE
WEREN'T PREPARED.

203
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,469
I'M SORRY I HAD TO TAKE

204
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:33,430
SUCH DRASTIC MEASURES
TO MAKE MY POINT

205
00:08:33,472 --> 00:08:35,807
BUT, LOOK, I JUST WANT
YOU GUYS TO BE SAFE.

206
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:36,808
OH.
OH.

207
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,852
DANGER!

208
00:08:42,356 --> 00:08:44,732
UH-HUH.

209
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:47,068
UNAGI.

210
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,660
2,000 BUCKS IS A LOT OF MONEY.

211
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:58,288
BOY, I WISH I HAD A TWIN.

212
00:08:58,330 --> 00:09:00,790
WHERE COULD I FIND SOMEONE...

213
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:04,127
WHO LOOKS EXACTLY LIKE ME?

214
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:25,732
HEY.

215
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,192
CHANDLER...

216
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:31,029
I SENSED IT WAS YOU.

217
00:09:32,489 --> 00:09:34,115
WHAT?

218
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:37,744
UNAGI.

219
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,704
I'M ALWAYS AWARE.

220
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:42,957
OKAY, ARE YOU AWARE
THAT UNAGI IS AN EEL?

221
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:45,668
WHAT'S UP?

222
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,546
I CAN'T FIGURE OUT
WHAT TO MAKE MONICA.

223
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:49,339
WHY NOT MAKE HER ONE
OF YOUR LITTLE JOKES?

224
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:50,840
I'M GOING CRAZY, OKAY?

225
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:52,967
DO YOU HAVE ANYTHING
AROUND HERE

226
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,344
THAT LOOKS HOMEMADE?

227
00:09:54,386 --> 00:09:55,678
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

228
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,764
SHE'D LOVE THIS.

229
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,807
IT'S AN EXACT REPLICA
OF APOLLO EIGHT.

230
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,476
I MADE IT IN THE SIXTH GRADE.

231
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:03,103
YEAH, I GUESS
I COULD USE THAT.

232
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:05,480
I COULD SAY, "YOUR LOVE
SENDS ME TO THE MOON."

233
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:06,981
YEAH, YEAH.

234
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:10,277
EXCEPT APOLLO EIGHT DIDN'T
ACTUALLY LAND ON THE MOON.

235
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:11,611
BUT YOU COULD WRITE

236
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:14,030
"YOUR LOVE LETS ME
ORBIT THE MOON TWICE

237
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:16,283
AND RETURN SAFELY."

238
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:18,785
WAIT A MINUTE, I CAN'T
GIVE THIS TO HER.

239
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:20,120
WHY NOT?

240
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:22,330
BECAUSE IT SAYS "CAPTAIN
ROSS" ON THE SIDE...

241
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,833
AND IT SAYS "I HATE
MONICA" ON THE BOTTOM.

242
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:26,876
MM-HMM.

243
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,506
DANGER!
DANGER!

244
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:33,550
( high-pitched shriek )

245
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,848
AH...

246
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,101
SALMON SKIN ROLL.

247
00:10:46,938 --> 00:10:48,940
OKAY... OKAY...

248
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:05,790
YES, HONEY, I'VE MADE IT MYSELF.

249
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,930
I CAN'T DO IT.
I CAN'T DO IT.

250
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:25,852
OH! OH!

251
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,895
A MIX TAPE! A MIX TAPE!

252
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,232
OKAY, HI.

253
00:11:31,274 --> 00:11:32,775
UH, YOU READY TO
EXCHANGE GIFTS?

254
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:33,818
SURE.

255
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,111
OKAY, YOU GO FIRST.

256
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,571
OKAY, COME HERE.
COME HERE.

257
00:11:36,613 --> 00:11:38,031
OKAY.
NOW, IT'S NOT WRAPPED

258
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,616
BECAUSE I JUST,
JUST FINISHED IT.

259
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:40,617
OKAY.

260
00:11:40,659 --> 00:11:42,619
BUT I MADE YOU A TAPE

261
00:11:42,661 --> 00:11:45,079
OF WHAT I THINK
ARE ALL ROMANTIC SONGS.

262
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,540
( gasping )

263
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,375
WHAT A GREAT GIFT.

264
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,587
IS "THE WAY YOU LOOK
TONIGHT" ON IT?

265
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,176
MAYBE. WE'LL HAVE
TO LISTEN AND SEE.

266
00:11:58,218 --> 00:11:59,594
OH, I LOVE IT.

267
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,095
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

268
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,263
OKAY.

269
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:03,264
OKAY.

270
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:04,391
YOU READY TO
OPEN YOURS?

271
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,933
YEAH.
OKAY.

272
00:12:17,654 --> 00:12:19,364
IT'S A SOCK BUNNY.

273
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:22,200
YEAH, YEAH, YOU REMEMBER
HOW I CALL YOU "BUNNY"?

274
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:24,911
NOT REALLY.

275
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:26,913
WELL, I DID ONE TIME

276
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:29,207
AND I WANT TO START
DOING IT MORE.

277
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:32,544
SEE, THAT'S WHAT
THIS IS ABOUT.
I SEE.

278
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:35,129
YOU KNOW, UM...
PHOEBE MAKES SOCK BUNNIES.

279
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,506
NO, NO, SHE DOESN'T.

280
00:12:36,548 --> 00:12:38,592
PHOEBE, WHAT SHE MAKES,
THEY'RE SOCK RABBITS.

281
00:12:38,633 --> 00:12:40,051
THEY'RE COMPLETELY
DIFFERENT.

282
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:41,720
OKAY! OKAY!

283
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,761
OKAY

284
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:44,097
I DIDN'T MAKE IT.

285
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:45,806
I'M SORRY.
I TOTALLY FORGOT ABOUT TONIGHT

286
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:47,808
AND THE FACT THAT WE'RE
SUPPOSED TO MAKE THE PRESENTS.

287
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,310
OH, IT'S OKAY. I DON'T, I...

288
00:12:49,352 --> 00:12:50,978
NO, NO, IT'S NOT OKAY.
IT'S NOT.

289
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,189
I MEAN, YOU WERE JUST...
YOU'RE SO INCREDIBLE

290
00:12:53,231 --> 00:12:54,982
AND YOU WENT THROUGH
ALL THIS TIME AND EFFORT TO MAKE

291
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:58,403
THIS TAPE FOR ME;
YOU KNOW, I'M
JUST GOING TO...

292
00:12:58,445 --> 00:13:02,073
I'M GOING TO HAVE TO MAKE
THIS UP TO YOU-- I WILL.

293
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:05,910
I AM GOING TO... COOK YOU
ANYTHING YOU WANT IN HERE

294
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:09,414
AND I'M GOING TO DO
ANYTHING YOU WANT IN THERE.

295
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:14,461
WELL, I DID PUT
A LOT OF THOUGHT INTO THE TAPE.

296
00:13:25,138 --> 00:13:26,347
WOW.

297
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:32,353
YOU ARE WAY TOO YOUNG
TO HAVE SEEN THAT.

298
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:36,483
YOU KNOW, YOUR BIRTHDAY'S
IN A MONTH AND A HALF.

299
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,858
WHAT DO YOU SAY

300
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,278
I FORGET TO GET YOU
A PRESENT FOR THAT TOO?

301
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:44,282
YOU ARE TOTALLY AND
COMPLETELY 100% FORGIVEN.

302
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:46,033
WE HAVE GOT TO WASH THAT.

303
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:47,118
YEAH.

304
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:51,706
HEY.

305
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,667
DO YOU REMEMBER THAT JACKET
THAT YOU LOVED SO MUCH

306
00:13:53,708 --> 00:13:55,251
THAT YOU THOUGHT
WAS TOO EXPENSIVE?

307
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,462
YOU HAVE DONE ENOUGH.

308
00:13:57,504 --> 00:14:00,131
I'M GOING TO WAKE UP EARLY
AND GO GET IT FOR YOU.

309
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:02,592
NO, YOU DON'T HAVE... GET
IT IN BLACK, NOT BROWN.

310
00:14:02,634 --> 00:14:03,842
( bell dings )

311
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:06,095
OOP! YOUR CAKE IS READY.

312
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:07,221
OOP.

313
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:11,934
WELL, IT'S LIKE
THAT OLD SAYING--

314
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:14,729
"HAVE SEX,
EAT SOME CAKE."

315
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:19,233
HEY, MON. HEY, CHAN.

316
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:20,568
JUST GETTING A SODA.

317
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:27,283
WHO THE HELL ARE YOU?

318
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:29,118
I'M JOEY.

319
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:32,664
HOW ARE YOU DOIN'?

320
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:37,126
NO! NO! NO! NO! NO!

321
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:38,877
HOW YOU DOIN'?

322
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:41,548
HOW YOU DOIN'?

323
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:43,216
DAMN IT, CARL.
GO WAIT IN THE HALL.

324
00:14:48,471 --> 00:14:49,848
LOOK.

325
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,058
I'VE GOT TO APOLOGIZE
ON BEHALF OF CARL.

326
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:54,561
WHO THE HELL IS CARL?!

327
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,354
OH, DID I NOT MENTION?

328
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:58,147
CARL

329
00:14:58,189 --> 00:15:00,483
IS A GUY I HIRED
TO BE MY IDENTICAL TWIN

330
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,318
FOR A MEDICAL RESEARCH
PROJECT.

331
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,490
YOU KNOW, SOMETIMES
THE GOOD IDEAS ARE

332
00:15:07,532 --> 00:15:09,659
JUST RIGHT IN FRONT
OF YOU, AREN'T THEY?

333
00:15:09,701 --> 00:15:12,620
I KNOW IT SOUNDS CRAZY,
BUT I THINK IT MIGHT WORK

334
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,997
BUT THE ONLY PROBLEM IS,
CARL'S ACTING IS...

335
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,500
THE ONLY PROBLEM?

336
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:19,043
YEAH, HE'S THE REASON
I DIDN'T GET

337
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:20,378
THAT BIG MINUTE MAID
COMMERCIAL

338
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,962
A COUPLE OF YEARS AGO,
REMEMBER?

339
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:24,507
WE WERE SUPPOSED TO BE BROTHERS,
BUT HE MESSED IT UP.

340
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:26,008
HEY.

341
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,968
UH, CAN I GET A LITTLE PIECE
OF THAT CAKE?

342
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,012
PIZZA! WE LIKE PIZZA!

343
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,097
GET OUT!

344
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,231
PAT SAJAK?

345
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,232
YEAH.

346
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:42,358
ALEX TREBEK?

347
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,359
OH, OF COURSE.

348
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:45,236
CHUCK WOOLERY.

349
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:46,529
DEFINITELY, PHOEBE.

350
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:49,365
YOU WILL NOT FIND
A SINGLE GAME SHOW HOST

351
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,367
WHOSE ASS I CANNOT KICK.

352
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,460
( groaning in pain )

353
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:01,628
SAY IT!

354
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,087
SAY "WE ARE UNAGI."

355
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:07,842
IT'S NOT SOMETHING YOU ARE;
IT'S SOMETHING YOU HAVE.

356
00:16:07,884 --> 00:16:09,844
SAY IT!

357
00:16:09,886 --> 00:16:12,221
YOU KNOW, I COULD EASILY
GET OUT OF THIS

358
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:15,892
BUT THERE'S A CHANCE
YOU COULD GET VERY, VERY HURT.

359
00:16:17,769 --> 00:16:19,312
( screaming )

360
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:29,530
ALL RIGHT, CARL, WE'RE NEXT.

361
00:16:29,572 --> 00:16:30,573
NOW REMEMBER

362
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:32,199
WHAT IS THIS
NOT GOING TO BE?

363
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:34,285
ANOTHER MINUTE
MAID FIASCO.

364
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:35,536
THAT'S RIGHT.

365
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,413
AND WHAT ARE YOU
NOT GOING TO DO?

366
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:38,915
I'M NOT GOING TO TALK BECAUSE...

367
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:41,000
THAT... DAMN IT, CARL!

368
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:43,461
( warning grunt )

369
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:47,089
CAN I HAVE THE NEXT ONE,
PLEASE?

370
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:49,258
THANK YOU.

371
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:51,385
JOEY AND TONY TRIBBIANI.

372
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:52,846
THAT'S US.

373
00:16:52,887 --> 00:16:54,263
BUT, UH...

374
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:56,557
THIS IS A STUDY
FOR IDENTICAL TWINS.

375
00:16:56,599 --> 00:17:00,227
THAT'S RIGHT--
$2,000.

376
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:02,647
BUT YOU'RE NOT IDENTICAL TWINS.

377
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:07,193
DAMN IT, CARL!

378
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:16,118
OH, MY GOOD GOD.

379
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:20,122
OKAY, CONTINUING
THE COUNTDOWN

380
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,749
OF YOUR FAVORITE MEALS.

381
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:25,169
TONIGHT, NUMBER THREE:

382
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:28,255
MACARONI AND CHEESE
WITH CUT-UP HOT DOGS.

383
00:17:29,883 --> 00:17:32,134
LOOK, YOU HAVE DONE
ENOUGH, OKAY?

384
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:34,012
YOU HAVE TO STOP THIS NOW.

385
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:36,055
I WILL BUT NOT TONIGHT.

386
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:37,431
AND FOR DINNER MUSIC,
I THOUGHT

387
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:40,518
WE COULD LISTEN TO THAT
TAPE THAT YOU MADE ME.

388
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,520
OH, THE MIX TAPE.

389
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:48,484
Tony Bennett:
♪ When I'm awfully low... ♪

390
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:53,990
"THE WAY YOU LOOK TONIGHT"
IS ON HERE.

391
00:17:54,032 --> 00:17:55,533
DANCE WITH ME?

392
00:17:55,575 --> 00:18:04,834
♪ I will feel a glow
just thinking of you ♪

393
00:18:04,876 --> 00:18:10,464
♪ And the way
you look tonight. ♪

394
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:17,179
YOU ARE JUST
THE SWEETEST...

395
00:18:18,848 --> 00:18:21,517
Janice:
I love the way you look

396
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:24,102
every night, Chandler.

397
00:18:28,983 --> 00:18:30,610
That's why I made you this tape.

398
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:33,071
Happy Birthday!

399
00:18:33,111 --> 00:18:34,864
Love, Janice.

400
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:35,907
( kissing sound )

401
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:43,247
NO, YOU'RE THE SWEETEST...

402
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:52,381
OKAY, LADIES, THAT ENDS TODAY'S
CLASS, AND LET'S REMEMBER--

403
00:18:52,423 --> 00:18:54,133
LET'S BE SAFE OUT THERE.

404
00:19:00,723 --> 00:19:01,933
IT'S A GREAT CLASS.

405
00:19:01,975 --> 00:19:03,017
THANKS, MAN.

406
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:05,103
YEAH, YEAH,
I WAS WATCHING.

407
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:10,524
UM, HEY, A COUPLE
OF QUESTIONS, THOUGH.

408
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,568
UM, YOU KNOW,
ABOUT THAT LAST MOVE

409
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:15,404
WHERE THAT WOMAN TRIPPED YOU
AND THEN PINNED YOU

410
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:16,697
TO THE FLOOR?

411
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:18,407
WHAT WOULD YOU DO NEXT?

412
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:20,743
WELL, AND THEN SHE'D TAKE
HER KEYS AND TRY TO JAM THEM...

413
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:23,913
NO, NO,
WHAT WOULD YOU DO NEXT?

414
00:19:23,955 --> 00:19:26,082
WHO, ME, THE ATTACKER?

415
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:27,583
YES, THAT'S RIGHT.

416
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:29,251
WHY?

417
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:31,253
I TRIED ATTACKING TWO WOMEN.

418
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,047
DID NOT WORK.

419
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,340
WHAT?

420
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:35,549
NO, I MEAN, IT'S OKAY.

421
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:37,176
I MEAN, THEY'RE MY FRIENDS.

422
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:39,887
IN FACT, I WAS MARRIED
TO ONE OF THEM.

423
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:41,179
LET ME GET
THIS STRAIGHT.

424
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,932
YOU ATTACKED YOUR EX-WIFE?

425
00:19:42,974 --> 00:19:45,768
OH, NO, NO, NO.

426
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:47,937
I TRIED

427
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:49,605
BUT I COULDN'T.

428
00:19:49,647 --> 00:19:51,774
THAT'S WHY I'M HERE.

429
00:19:53,109 --> 00:19:55,778
MAYBE WE COULD ATTACK THEM
TOGETHER.

430
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,406
THAT'S A "NO."

431
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:05,121
I AM SO, SO,
SO, SO SORRY.

432
00:20:05,163 --> 00:20:07,040
UH-HUH.

433
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:12,879
OH! AND I WILL COOK
ANYTHING YOU WANT IN HERE

434
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,716
AND DO ANYTHING YOU WANT
IN THERE.

435
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:20,761
YEAH, YOU WILL,
AND ARE YOU KIDDING ME?

436
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,559
OH, COME ON, MONICA,
IT'S OUR VALENTINE'S DAY.

437
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,895
PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE?

438
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:32,314
OKAY.

439
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:33,733
OKAY?

440
00:20:40,073 --> 00:20:42,075
Janice:
♪ My funny valentine... ♪

441
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:49,415
SO ARE WE GOING IN THERE?

442
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:51,125
I AM.

443
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,557
AHA.

444
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,227
NOWHERE TO RUN.

445
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,439
I DON'T LIKE
SITTING UP HERE.

446
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:14,774
I'M GOING OVER THERE.

447
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:16,234
NO, RACHEL,
THEY GOT HERE FIRST.

448
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,492
WHAT?

449
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:26,869
WHY IS ROSS DOING THAT?

450
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:28,121
Ross:
DANGER!

451
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:29,580
OH, MY GOD!

452
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:32,250
WHY IS HE JUMPING
ON THOSE WOMEN?

453
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:35,795
WE SHOULD HELP THEM.

454
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:38,672
I... I DON'T THINK
THEY NEED ANY HELP.

455
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:41,550
( screaming )

456
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:50,476
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

